Homepage: https://github.com/hugomonizdorego/Eduka-Lafa
Description: Lafa - encyclopedia of Timor-Leste and virtual assistant
 Lafa Desktop is an interactive encyclopedia of Timor-Leste, from the
 formation of the island to 2026: history, colonial times and the
 occupation, the State and its leaders, the flag and national symbols,
 culture, society, economy (exports, imports, coffee, oil and gas),
 land and nature, the 14 municipalities on an interactive map, tourist
 places, public holidays and national days, a "millionaire" quiz, more
 than 1000 Tetun words with their meaning in Portuguese, Indonesian,
 English and other ASEAN and CPLP languages, and learning paths for the
 school levels of the Ministry of Education. Texts are in Tetun,
 Portuguese, Indonesian and English, with sources and licences.
 .
 Everything works offline. With internet, Lafa can download Wikipedia
 introductions and free-licence photos for offline use, World Bank data
 and new content (checked with SHA-256). No login, no AI, no server.
 .
 The optional Lafa Virtual Assistant (switched on in Eduka-Settings ->
 Lafa-Configuration) is a Timor-Leste guide and study buddy on the
 Eduka-Panel: daily facts, holidays, Tetun words and mini quizzes.
